Subject: P6 revised - remove orphan Whiteboard UI, preserve legacy compatibility

Base: current working source, including the scene output-path, libass and Kinetic fixes.
This patch is an artifact only; it has not been applied to the working repository.

Scope:
- Remove only the unreferenced WhiteboardProject.tsx component.
- Preserve V1 commands/API/exporter and their tests until all old configurations can migrate.
- Import compatible legacy name/hand/masterAudio projects into the current editor in memory.
- Request Save As after migration; never rewrite a source file just by opening it.
- Reject unsupported legacy features explicitly rather than silently changing export behavior.
- Preserve the existing speechConfig and WB schema 2/3 import documentation.
- Keep all recent output-path, libass, Kinetic and thumbnail-offset fixes unchanged.

Migration limits: outputSize, custom hands, disabled scenes, mixed master/per-scene audio,
and discontinuous master timelines still use the retained V1 backend. Conversion to the
editor requires a new thumbnail and does not promise frame-identical legacy output.

Validated in an isolated copy:
- cargo test --lib --offline -- --skip secret_store::tests: 43 passed (keychain test excluded).
- npm run build: passed (existing dynamic-import warning remains).
- git apply --check against the current working repository: checked separately after generation.

